<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01TA">Remark <span data-tag="01TA">5.1.1.6</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow Y$ and $q: Y \rightarrow Z$ be morphisms of simplicial sets, and let $e$ be an edge of the simplicial set $X$. If $e$ is $p$-cartesian and $p(e)$ is a $q$-cartesian edge of $Y$, then $e$ is $(q \circ p)$-cartesian. For a partial converse, see Corollary <a data-tag="01TU" href="/tag/01TU">5.1.2.6</a>. </p>
</article>
